Sval: suppress permission prompts under an agent's overlay

An agent's overlay covers its window while the agent works there, and the
notification panel is a native popup drawn above it, where the user could
answer a page's permission prompt without taking control. Suppressed as a
tab dialog suppresses it, the prompt stays pending and shows once the
overlay goes. The suppression test is browser.js's own function, which the
panel's owner reads by name, so it is patched here.

diff --git a/browser/base/content/browser.js b/browser/base/content/browser.js
index c919cf5c91..cb1e577ce8 100644
--- a/browser/base/content/browser.js
+++ b/browser/base/content/browser.js
@@ -695,10 +695,13 @@ function shouldSuppressPopupNotifications() {
   // This can be removed once bug 545265 and bug 1320361 are fixed.
   // Hide popup notifications when system tab prompts are shown so they
   // don't cover up the prompt.
+  // Sval: and while an agent's overlay covers the window, which the
+  // notification panel would draw above.
   return (
     window.windowState == window.STATE_MINIMIZED ||
     gBrowser?.selectedBrowser.hasAttribute("tabDialogShowing") ||
-    gDialogBox?.isOpen
+    gDialogBox?.isOpen ||
+    document.documentElement.hasAttribute("sval-agent-overlay")
   );
 }
 
